1
00:01:11,330 --> 00:02:02,430
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:06,880
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:12,960
Yannis!

4
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,060
Where is Edebali?

5
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:28,320
- I'm here because he's not, Osman.
- Stop beating around the bush!

6
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:32,010
- Answer my question!
- Edebali and his daughter are gone.

7
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:36,010
But I don't know where they are.
It won't take too long.

8
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:39,140
Don't forget that you're in my hands.

9
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:43,560
Killing me is the last thing you want
right now, Osman.

10
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,140
Devil!

11
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:52,250
Selcan Hatun.

12
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:58,460
What are you talking about? Selcan Hatun
is not even in Söğüt.

13
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,980
Your anger has left your sense in
the shade, Osman.

14
00:03:02,230 --> 00:03:05,950
You're forgetting that we have hands
in every shadow.

15
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:10,040
What did you do to Selcan Hatun?

16
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:13,750
We will not decide on that. You will.

17
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:19,770
She is resting in the caravanserai,
unaware of everything.

18
00:03:51,570 --> 00:03:55,180
- Welcome, Princess Sofia.
- Thank you.

19
00:04:03,590 --> 00:04:05,960
What are you searching for, Selcan Hatun?

20
00:04:07,510 --> 00:04:11,510
My dagger is here, but I can't find
Mother Hayme's reminiscence.

21
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,780
You go, continue your meal.

22
00:04:33,810 --> 00:04:35,460
Yes, Princess?

23
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:40,460
To that table, send plenty of lamb
and fruits.

24
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:14,180
What gives, what are these?

25
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:18,250
Treats of Kulucahisar' Princess Sofia,
Selcan Hatun.

26
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:41,170
If I don't get out of here alive...

27
00:05:41,170 --> 00:05:46,260
... one of my men is waiting outside
to fly the news to the caravanserai.

28
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:11,830
Are you ready to negotiate with
your devil, Osman?

29
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,000
What do you want?

30
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,990
In return of my life, Selcan Hatun's life.

31
00:06:27,990 --> 00:06:30,070
You're lying!

32
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:35,100
You made this up to get out of my hands.

33
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:01,920
Thank you for accepting my treats.

34
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:08,400
It's not a holiday, nor a feast day.
What were the treats for, Hatun?

35
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:14,810
You're our guest here. Treats reflect
the host's respect and honour.

36
00:07:21,990 --> 00:07:24,250
May I sit?

37
00:07:28,910 --> 00:07:32,610
Dumb guests think they are the hosts.

38
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:38,830
This land is ours.
And about being a guest...

39
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:45,040
If you accept being a guest at my table,
go ahead and sit.

40
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:49,880
As you wish.

41
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:09,860
So you are that famous Selcan Hatun.

42
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:18,330
Even the wise Greek women of
Kulucahisar speak highly of you.

43
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:25,160
We look at the furnace, not the fire. If
our names are known, thanks to Mother Hayme.

44
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:29,650
I'm sure Mother Hayme's grandson...

45
00:08:30,970 --> 00:08:33,060
... Osman Bey...

46
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,750
... will be very happy to see you.

47
00:08:43,990 --> 00:08:47,230
Being related is divine for us, Princess.

48
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:50,360
But Osman is like a son to me.

49
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:54,320
I too, of course, missed him a lot.

50
00:09:00,970 --> 00:09:03,100
Tell me.

51
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,650
Why do you have ties with Osman?

52
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:19,770
Osman Bey found my husband's
killers and punished them.

53
00:09:19,770 --> 00:09:24,420
In our eyes, he is rather valuable.

54
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:39,390
Does this dagger look familiar, Osman?

55
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,380
Mother Hayme!

56
00:09:47,190 --> 00:09:53,230
If you decline my offer, Selcan Hatun
will be needing this dagger very much.

57
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:57,870
She's like a mother to me.
If you hurt her...

58
00:09:57,870 --> 00:10:02,030
... I'll take you even if you are in a well
full of snakes with my bare hands!

59
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:08,560
It's not over yet Osman.
Not only my life...

60
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:11,830
... I'll also give you Aybar's killers.

61
00:10:14,460 --> 00:10:18,870
But then, of course, you'll be
silent during my execution.

62
00:10:25,470 --> 00:10:28,960
- Selcan Hatun.
- Will be at the Tent safe and sound.

63
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:35,200
Now think carefully. You either go to the
castle and witness my execution...

64
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:41,960
Or return to the castle after taking
Aybars' revenge...

65
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:47,020
... and reunite with Selcan Hatun
you love as a mother.

66
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:50,840
This was a big trick, wasn't it?

67
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:55,710
Only I know you well.

68
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,860
You'll fake your death and disappear.

69
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:05,630
Now, this is the Osman Bey I know!

70
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:09,400
Both brave and intelligent.

71
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:11,630
Don't forget that I also show no mercy!

72
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:16,570
I... I'm a dead man Osman.

73
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,620
Where are Aybars' killers?

74
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:29,920
They are in the Dark Woods now.
And their leader...

75
00:11:30,990 --> 00:11:33,790
... is Salvador.

76
00:11:47,430 --> 00:11:49,450
Osman Bey!

77
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:54,180
Make haste! I don't even know...

78
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,260
... who will they hurt next.

79
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:00,660
This is not over, Yannis.

80
00:12:01,870 --> 00:12:06,980
Your dark shadows, your bat-like face...

81
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:10,210
... will be drowned in the light of
my sword. Know that.

82
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:30,700
For our cause and Master Yannis.

83
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:44,230
For our cause and Master Yannis.

84
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:05,370
Thanks to Osman Bey, we cut down a big
tumour of these lands.

85
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:13,930
As much of a clumsy hunter, Osman Bey
proved that he'll be a great Bey.

86
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,840
Why isn't Osman here?

87
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:27,350
You had to know that, Bamsı Bey.

88
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:34,510
Sofia isn't here either.
Gündüz Bey, something is wrong here.

89
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:40,910
Once Osman is here, we'll figure it out.

90
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:49,030
So, where is Osman, Dündar Bey?

91
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:53,440
Who can find sense in Osman's
business, Alişar Bey?

92
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:57,970
Next thing you know, he's here.

93
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:07,300
So, how do we know that this
corpse is that Yannis guy?

94
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:10,030
What if he isn't?

95
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:15,260
The only one who knows him other
than us is Osman.

96
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:21,670
And he didn't come to the execution.
Trust us, Bamsı Bey.

97
00:14:26,070 --> 00:14:31,120
Even the corpse of someone like Yannis
will cause air pollution.

98
00:14:33,290 --> 00:14:35,110
Take him away.

99
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:55,320
Alişar Bey. While you are here, we wish
to renew our old agreement.

100
00:14:58,210 --> 00:14:59,960
After you, Alişar Bey.

101
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:02,720
Dündar Bey.

102
00:15:19,170 --> 00:15:23,320
Gündüz, I don't feel at ease at all.

103
00:15:23,330 --> 00:15:27,010
Your uncle is still running
after agreements.

104
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:29,240
And Osman isn't anywhere to be seen.

105
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:35,260
Don't you worry Bamsı Bey. My father Ertuğrul
Gazi laid the foundations of this agreement.

106
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:39,500
Ertuğrul Bey wanted to do this
agreement with Yorgopolos.

107
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:45,080
Not with these nasty ones. Gündüz Bey.
Not with these nasty ones.

108
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:53,360
Not with these. Where are you my Osman?
Where?

109
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:41,940
Congrats. You look like you
just heard some good news.

110
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:47,640
Thank God they took care of a matter that
would have costed countless lives.

111
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:50,220
You brought luck.

112
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:57,670
Thank you for your hospitality.

113
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:05,190
Pleasure to meet you.

114
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:12,910
If you allow me, I'd like to visit
you and Zöhre Hatun in your Tent.

115
00:17:12,910 --> 00:17:17,790
Of course. Our doors are
always open to friendlies.

116
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:11,380
Aybüke, who are they?

117
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,920
I don't know, Selcan Hatun.

118
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:25,800
My lovely girl, where are you from?
Where do you come from, where do you go?

119
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:30,980
With Ahi Evran's follower Ahis, we are
the fellow sisters of Fatma Bacı, mother.

120
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:37,540
Who is the magnificent one?

121
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:45,000
My Father Sheikh Edebali.

122
00:18:52,010 --> 00:18:55,950
If I were to go up to him, would
he be disturbed?

123
00:18:55,950 --> 00:19:00,940
My father likes to pray and to receive
prayer. He will be pleased.

124
00:19:01,860 --> 00:19:07,710
How gorgeous! You shine like the
moon, my sweet girl. Go on, light my way.

125
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:22,890
Don't mention it, Hatun.

126
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:29,190
If you allowed it, I would have shown you
my gratitudes, Efendi.

127
00:19:31,710 --> 00:19:38,040
Manners aren't licking a mortals boots,
Hatun.

128
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:45,220
Manners are knowing where you stand
before the creator's glory.

129
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:53,000
Praise be! They don't call you the
Turkmen's father for nothing.

130
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:57,970
You entered the caravanserai with your
light, shook with your greatness...

131
00:19:57,970 --> 00:20:00,410
... burnt with your wisdom.

132
00:20:04,230 --> 00:20:06,540
Excuse me.

133
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:09,670
Would you mind telling us your name?

134
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:19,200
A martyr's mother, another martyr's wife,
Selcan Hatun from the Kayı.

135
00:21:22,470 --> 00:21:25,570
Be careful just in case, brothers.

136
00:21:31,410 --> 00:21:32,880
- Bora!
- Yes, my Bey.

137
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:36,500
You, Kanturalı and Boğaç, watch the
right side.

138
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:40,930
- Don't let anyone run away.
- As you wish, my Bey.

139
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:43,170
Come on.

140
00:21:51,530 --> 00:21:57,160
Onur. With Demirbüken and Erkut, watch
the backside.

141
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:01,450
We'll attack on my mark.

142
00:22:13,130 --> 00:22:17,130
From now on, we don't have covers for
our swords on our backs.

143
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:24,690
There is anger to scare the enemy, venom
to infect the cruel.

144
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:29,190
Either death or victory.

145
00:22:51,050 --> 00:22:53,500
So, we'll burn Samsa' Tent.

146
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:59,900
We have arrived. From now on, only the
Angel of Death will wander in these lands.

147
00:23:47,810 --> 00:23:50,460
You know that I lost my wife.

148
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:58,530
If you allow it, I would like to
marry your daughter Aygül.

149
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:16,780
Alişar Bey. Dündar Bey.

150
00:24:16,780 --> 00:24:23,500
Sorry for making you wait. But the
agreement texts you were waiting for...

151
00:24:23,510 --> 00:24:25,760
... are ready.

152
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:31,260
Now that the traitor Yannis is dead...

153
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:35,760
... nothing is stopping us from
sealing the agreement.

154
00:24:37,730 --> 00:24:45,400
Will the agreement made while Osman isn't
here be valid? Dündar Bey.

155
00:24:48,790 --> 00:24:53,600
On our ways, elders talk, the little
ones stay silent.

156
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:59,230
About the agreement. With my
brother's word...

157
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:04,360
... I have the seal.

158
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:17,650
- Dündar Bey.
- Princess Sofia.

159
00:25:24,250 --> 00:25:28,890
One day I saw a really nice flower on the
shores of the Caspian.

160
00:25:31,520 --> 00:25:33,960
I can still smell it.

161
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:38,880
Every time I see you, I remember
that flower.

162
00:25:42,660 --> 00:25:45,380
And how poisonous it was.

163
00:27:32,080 --> 00:27:33,770
Boran!

164
00:28:01,620 --> 00:28:03,430
Where is Salvador?

165
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:08,420
Where is Salvador?

166
00:28:10,180 --> 00:28:14,120
Don't take the trouble, Osman Bey.
He'll find you.

167
00:28:16,540 --> 00:28:20,530
That demon Yannis who was hurting our
relationship got what was coming to him.

168
00:28:20,530 --> 00:28:24,480
Now it's time to make our friendship
everlasting.

169
00:28:26,940 --> 00:28:28,870
But...

170
00:28:28,870 --> 00:28:33,110
... you tried to make an agreement
without me.

171
00:28:35,170 --> 00:28:37,800
And you had a run of bad luck.

172
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:43,020
In these lands, no flower can blossom...

173
00:28:43,020 --> 00:28:45,810
... without Alişar Bey's permission.

174
00:28:52,710 --> 00:28:59,240
Now let's honour my deceased
husband Yorgopolos all together.

175
00:29:00,020 --> 00:29:02,720
We shall renew the agreement.

176
00:29:04,540 --> 00:29:09,470
Let's finish what Dündar Bey started
together.

177
00:29:10,570 --> 00:29:17,770
Also, different from the old one, the
perfume matter Dündar Bey wanted...

178
00:29:18,510 --> 00:29:20,770
... has also been added to the agreement.

179
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:55,550
Are the articles we want in the agreement?

180
00:29:55,830 --> 00:29:57,830
They are, Dündar Bey.

181
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:02,900
Alişar Bey, you look you you don't
trust us.

182
00:30:02,900 --> 00:30:05,670
You're reading it very carefully.

183
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:22,470
A man with no care is a man with
no dignity, Kalonoz.

184
00:31:02,770 --> 00:31:06,330
You'll pay for what you did to Aybars!

185
00:31:09,090 --> 00:31:14,430
You'll pay for what you did to Aybars!
You will pay for it!

186
00:31:24,190 --> 00:31:28,540
You can go. We'll inform you once
they talk.

187
00:31:28,750 --> 00:31:30,630
- Boran.
- Yes, Bey.

188
00:31:30,630 --> 00:31:34,960
My aunt Selcan is here. I need to go to
the Tent immediately.

189
00:31:38,020 --> 00:31:40,930
Take this dog to our place.

190
00:31:40,930 --> 00:31:44,960
- Make him talk until the morning.
- Don't you worry, my Bey.

191
00:31:45,710 --> 00:31:49,520
He'll talk eventually.

192
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:56,430
Sergeant Samsa, you return to your Tent.
Wait for my word.

193
00:32:40,090 --> 00:32:42,730
Welcome, Selcan Hatun!

194
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:03,340
Selcan Hatun.

195
00:33:17,820 --> 00:33:21,010
That's all we needed among all
these troubles.

196
00:33:25,690 --> 00:33:30,500
Good heavens! I saw Selcan Hatun with
my own eyes once again.

197
00:33:48,330 --> 00:33:49,970
Ayşe.

198
00:33:51,040 --> 00:33:53,320
My Aunt. Welcome.

199
00:33:56,630 --> 00:33:58,540
My sweet girl.

200
00:34:00,940 --> 00:34:04,070
- Welcome, Aunt Selcan.
- My Aygül.

201
00:34:04,980 --> 00:34:08,780
- Welcome Selcan Hatun.
- Thank you.

202
00:34:10,790 --> 00:34:13,550
Welcome, Selcan Hatun.

203
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:19,010
What happened, Zöhre?
Your face turned pale.

204
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:23,870
We're surprised, Hatun.
It's nice to have you back.

205
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:28,870
Where is my dark-eyed Osman?

206
00:34:33,290 --> 00:34:38,570
I've heard. Tell me. You put my
Osman in cages.

207
00:34:40,260 --> 00:34:43,120
Looks like trees started talking.

208
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:49,330
All beings start talking before
Selcan Hatun. Don't you know it, Zöhre?

209
00:34:51,080 --> 00:34:54,340
Stop beating around the bush and tell me.
Where is my Osman?

210
00:34:55,290 --> 00:34:58,970
Dündar Bey said the cage would tame him
but...

211
00:34:58,970 --> 00:35:01,710
... he punished himself.

212
00:35:01,710 --> 00:35:04,080
He tamed himself.

213
00:35:04,080 --> 00:35:07,520
Now, only Allah knows where he is.

214
00:35:11,730 --> 00:35:15,080
We couldn't keep up with him when he
was a little kid.

215
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:17,420
I'm sure he knows what he's doing.

216
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:24,330
Aygül. Bring me some ayran.
My heart is all dry.

217
00:35:24,330 --> 00:35:26,150
Right away, aunt Selcan.

218
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:32,230
Go ahead.

219
00:36:11,070 --> 00:36:13,150
Go ahead, Selcan Hatun.

220
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:35,960
You established your Tent on the
shadow of Ertuğrul Bey's Tent.

221
00:36:36,770 --> 00:36:41,570
But don't you know, no grass grows on
his Tent's shadow.

222
00:36:44,080 --> 00:36:49,800
Even though it's not a Tent worthy of
Dündar Bey, we keep on living, thankfully.

223
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:55,930
I hope Allah blesses you and your
loved ones with long lives.

224
00:36:55,930 --> 00:36:58,050
- Amen.
- Amen.

225
00:36:59,710 --> 00:37:04,860
Winter is near.
People don't migrate in these seasons.

226
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:08,180
Is it good or bad, Selcan Hatun?

227
00:37:08,180 --> 00:37:11,170
Only Allah knows that, Zöhre.

228
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:15,890
What gives, are you afraid we'll
disturb you?

229
00:37:16,700 --> 00:37:21,740
Not at all. I worry about you.

230
00:37:21,740 --> 00:37:24,170
I hope nothing is wrong.

231
00:37:25,060 --> 00:37:29,060
I'm tired, Zöhre. My Tent is also tired.

232
00:37:30,470 --> 00:37:34,740
After my Gündoğdu passed away,
I can't stay there.

233
00:37:34,740 --> 00:37:40,320
I have arrived. My Tent will be on the
road eventually.

234
00:37:41,120 --> 00:37:42,880
Inshallah.

235
00:39:28,660 --> 00:39:31,270
Who are these strangers?

236
00:39:32,310 --> 00:39:37,470
Not strangers, Bamsı Bey. They are snakes.
Snakes.

237
00:39:46,750 --> 00:39:48,360
On me...

238
00:39:51,790 --> 00:39:55,900
You have something on me that's
tiring my shoulders, Bamsı Bey.

239
00:39:59,400 --> 00:40:02,480
These little devils...

240
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:04,960
... are my brother Aybars' killers.

241
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:19,720
They also have a leader.
I'll also bring him to you.

242
00:40:21,390 --> 00:40:25,040
That old guy wasn't Yannis. Was he?

243
00:40:25,040 --> 00:40:28,730
He's the head of the snake.
I caught him from the tail.

244
00:40:28,730 --> 00:40:31,890
We'll crush his head eventually.

245
00:40:31,890 --> 00:40:34,050
Don't you worry.

246
00:40:39,620 --> 00:40:42,250
Now...

247
00:40:42,250 --> 00:40:46,240
Taking revenge is your job, not
mine, Bamsı Bey.

248
00:41:41,190 --> 00:41:46,890
Their blood can flow like
the Alaca River...

249
00:41:48,450 --> 00:41:52,360
... that still wouldn't ease my pain.

250
00:41:55,220 --> 00:42:00,920
My Osman. May you live long!
May you live long.

251
00:42:05,450 --> 00:42:08,360
I was wrong about you, Osman Bey.

252
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:10,980
I thought you had forgotten about Aybars.

253
00:42:10,980 --> 00:42:15,700
In our friendship, forgetting is
not a thing, Burçin Hatun.

254
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:38,520
Bamsı Bey.

255
00:43:17,630 --> 00:43:20,590
People!

256
00:43:20,590 --> 00:43:22,510
Brothers!

257
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:27,720
Sisters! Friends!

258
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:33,200
Today is the day
the fire inside me cools down!

259
00:43:34,890 --> 00:43:40,600
Today is the day I take my martyr
son Aybars' revenge!

260
00:43:46,330 --> 00:43:49,770
These snakes thought...

261
00:43:49,770 --> 00:43:53,690
... we would forget about our pain
and not go after it!

262
00:43:54,830 --> 00:43:59,010
The snakes thought
we don't seek revenge!

263
00:44:00,970 --> 00:44:04,140
But...

264
00:44:04,140 --> 00:44:09,990
... my dear Osman, with his claws
like an eagle...

265
00:44:09,990 --> 00:44:13,860
... took them and brought them to me!

266
00:44:16,720 --> 00:44:24,430
Now it's my turn to separate their
poisonous heads from their tails.

267
00:44:40,830 --> 00:44:43,130
In the name of Allah!

268
00:44:58,480 --> 00:45:00,700
Allahu Akbar!
(Allah is the Greatest)

269
00:45:01,820 --> 00:45:04,200
Allahu Akbar!
(Allah is the Greatest)

270
00:45:04,200 --> 00:45:12,220
Long live Osman Bey! Long live Bamsı Bey.

271
00:45:12,220 --> 00:45:33,500
www.kurulusosman.online

272
00:45:36,080 --> 00:45:42,650
This is the day we cut the heads of
all the snakes...

273
00:45:42,650 --> 00:45:45,380
... trying to slither into
the Turks heart!

274
00:45:46,220 --> 00:45:50,390
It's time to, with our faith...

275
00:45:50,390 --> 00:45:53,270
... march towards Kızıl Elma!

276
00:46:06,380 --> 00:46:09,800
My dark-eyed, valiant Osman!

277
00:46:18,170 --> 00:46:22,510
- Welcome, aunt.
- Thank you.

278
00:46:22,510 --> 00:46:27,220
When I saw you, I saw the welcome
ones, pleased ones, son.

279
00:46:28,650 --> 00:46:32,440
Come, we shall go to my father's Tent.

280
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:52,010
He found the governors killer. He found
Aybars' killers and brought them to the Tent.

281
00:46:54,500 --> 00:46:57,570
Osman is like a gurgling waterfall.

282
00:46:58,780 --> 00:47:02,780
Either we stand in his way to stop him...

283
00:47:03,290 --> 00:47:06,710
... or he will flood us all.

284
00:47:44,400 --> 00:47:49,940
His father's lion!
Kayı's prosperity, my Osman.

285
00:47:55,360 --> 00:48:00,410
Osman, don't let your eyelashes
cover your eyes.

286
00:48:01,710 --> 00:48:05,420
Tell me what bothers you.

287
00:48:05,640 --> 00:48:09,090
You are alive and well, aunt.

288
00:48:10,550 --> 00:48:13,710
This takes my anxiety away.
Thank Allah.

289
00:48:14,590 --> 00:48:17,160
Have a seat.

290
00:48:32,480 --> 00:48:39,340
Oh, my Osman. Your dreams will come true.
Kayı Tents are going to unite.

291
00:48:39,340 --> 00:48:45,790
Someday, all the Oghuz tents will be
strong and united.

292
00:48:46,920 --> 00:48:50,850
In sha Allah, my lion.
In sha Allah.

293
00:48:52,560 --> 00:48:56,790
I heard that you went to the caravanserai.
(A roadside hotel for travellers in old times.)

294
00:48:56,790 --> 00:48:58,450
Yes, I did.

295
00:48:59,220 --> 00:49:01,570
I hope nothing's wrong.

296
00:49:11,020 --> 00:49:13,150
Osman.

297
00:49:13,630 --> 00:49:16,080
Where did you find this dagger?

298
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:20,290
Was there anyone who drew your attention
in the caravanserai?

299
00:49:22,260 --> 00:49:24,550
Yes.

300
00:49:25,070 --> 00:49:30,300
Princess of Kulucahisar came to me.

301
00:49:31,150 --> 00:49:35,350
- Sofia.
- Sofia.

302
00:49:36,270 --> 00:49:41,380
But, what does Sofia have to do with
this dagger, son?

303
00:49:42,460 --> 00:49:49,270
They want me to forgive someone's life
in return of your life, aunt.

304
00:49:49,270 --> 00:49:51,600
You don't say!

305
00:49:51,950 --> 00:49:53,930
Is it Sofia?

306
00:49:54,850 --> 00:49:56,850
Yannis.

307
00:49:57,220 --> 00:49:59,460
Who is Yannis?

308
00:50:00,280 --> 00:50:03,230
- We will talk about it in the evening, aunt.
- My Osman...

309
00:50:03,270 --> 00:50:10,360
When I was at the caravanserai,
I met Sheikh Edebalı.

310
00:50:10,720 --> 00:50:13,100
Are you serious, aunt?

311
00:50:15,500 --> 00:50:19,890
Your face is shining like the moon,
my lion. What happened?

312
00:50:21,880 --> 00:50:26,260
You gave me very important news.
What about his daughter?

313
00:50:27,810 --> 00:50:29,520
Was his daughter with him?

314
00:50:29,520 --> 00:50:31,880
- Do you mean Bala Hatun?
- Yes.

315
00:50:31,880 --> 00:50:36,780
Of course.
I met her too.

316
00:50:40,010 --> 00:50:42,310
Where are you going?

317
00:50:42,320 --> 00:50:45,390
I have to go to the caravanserai
immediately, aunt.

318
00:50:45,390 --> 00:50:49,670
We have a lot of things to talk about
this evening.

319
00:51:25,420 --> 00:51:30,550
I have never thought that my death would
amuse them that much.

320
00:51:35,380 --> 00:51:37,400
Edebali.

321
00:51:37,780 --> 00:51:42,820
- He'll believe you are dead, sir.
- So, he'll make his moves more comfortably.

322
00:51:46,950 --> 00:51:53,140
If it was so easy, I would have already
died until now.

323
00:51:59,810 --> 00:52:02,240
Prince Salvador!

324
00:52:08,190 --> 00:52:11,540
Osman is trapped, sir.

325
00:52:11,540 --> 00:52:15,830
Now it's the big wolf's turn.

326
00:52:16,470 --> 00:52:22,460
I thought you would be sorry for your
warriors, Prince Salvador!

327
00:52:23,690 --> 00:52:29,010
Only digressing from my ideas
can upset me, Commander.

328
00:52:35,450 --> 00:52:39,810
- Do we have a destination, sir?
- Yes, of course.

329
00:52:40,750 --> 00:52:44,790
Our destination is the straight path.

330
00:52:44,790 --> 00:52:47,920
- Of course, sir.
- Of course, sir.

331
00:52:48,980 --> 00:52:51,310
My dear friends.

332
00:52:51,310 --> 00:52:57,580
To remain a Muslim is more important
than being born a Muslim.

333
00:52:57,880 --> 00:53:04,220
They can torture us, they can banish
us from our land.

334
00:53:04,220 --> 00:53:09,310
Even a scholar can't teach
an ignorant person.

335
00:53:09,320 --> 00:53:12,210
We will keep on going.

336
00:53:13,060 --> 00:53:17,370
We are not going to change our
destination.

337
00:53:18,600 --> 00:53:20,810
Remember this, friends.

338
00:53:21,860 --> 00:53:29,330
Whoever obeys abasement will be awarded
with dignity and greatness.

339
00:53:29,330 --> 00:53:31,720
- Eyvallah (thank you) sir.
- Eyvallah (thank you) sir.

340
00:53:32,010 --> 00:53:36,870
Sir, they say Yannis has been killed.

341
00:53:36,900 --> 00:53:39,900
A mouse sees a piece of bread.

342
00:53:39,910 --> 00:53:47,000
The mouse looks at both where he stands
and where the bread is.

343
00:53:48,150 --> 00:53:51,040
And he says "there's something wrong."

344
00:53:51,260 --> 00:53:56,940
"The bread is big.
Also, the distance is too short."

345
00:53:57,260 --> 00:53:59,410
What do you suspect, sir?

346
00:54:00,170 --> 00:54:03,780
Yannis is a big bait.

347
00:54:03,780 --> 00:54:08,660
Besides, it is weird that he is gone
easily.

348
00:54:09,020 --> 00:54:17,120
In my opinion, a girl like Sofia never
accepts his father's execution.

349
00:54:17,360 --> 00:54:22,110
- Their intention is clear.
- Only you know the place of the treasure.

350
00:54:22,280 --> 00:54:25,210
- They know this, don't they?
- Yes.

351
00:54:25,210 --> 00:54:26,800
They do.

352
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:30,810
That's why they are going to trap Osman.

353
00:54:31,030 --> 00:54:36,620
They are going to aim to confuse him,
to change his mind.

354
00:54:38,400 --> 00:54:42,930
Did Osman go to the execution ceremony?

355
00:54:43,270 --> 00:54:44,670
He didn't, sir.

356
00:54:46,280 --> 00:54:50,150
So, the devil started to confuse him.

357
00:54:50,150 --> 00:54:56,090
When he talks with Selcan Hatun,
he will come to you, sir.

358
00:54:56,100 --> 00:54:59,150
He will want to see you.

359
00:55:10,680 --> 00:55:14,500
- Peace be with you.
- Peace be with you.

360
00:55:16,910 --> 00:55:21,460
Can you notify Edebali that I want to see
him, Dervish?

361
00:55:21,480 --> 00:55:23,020
Eyvallah (okay).

362
00:55:23,030 --> 00:55:24,760
Osman Bey.

363
00:55:30,920 --> 00:55:33,210
Bala Hatun.

364
00:55:36,700 --> 00:55:39,480
Thank Allah, I've found you.

365
00:55:47,580 --> 00:55:50,900
I was worried because you left the tent
suddenly.

366
00:55:52,350 --> 00:55:56,750
Is your father angry with me?

367
00:55:57,840 --> 00:56:00,680
He sensed it, Osman Bey.

368
00:56:02,780 --> 00:56:06,810
I know, it was my bad.
I disappointed him.

369
00:56:09,630 --> 00:56:15,400
I came here to seek forgiveness.

370
00:56:17,330 --> 00:56:20,570
My father doesn't turn away anyone who
comes to him, Osman Bey.

371
00:56:21,190 --> 00:56:27,530
Also, he is upset about what you did.
He wants to guide you.

372
00:56:28,470 --> 00:56:33,520
He is our light.

373
00:56:34,280 --> 00:56:37,210
I didn't want to upset him.

374
00:56:37,880 --> 00:56:40,770
Do you know why you upset my father?

375
00:56:43,990 --> 00:56:46,280
I know, Bala Hatun.

376
00:56:49,030 --> 00:56:55,200
I tried to be the justice instead of
fighting for justice.

377
00:56:57,900 --> 00:57:00,200
That's right.

378
00:57:00,560 --> 00:57:03,000
He'll be happy to see you.

379
00:57:03,400 --> 00:57:07,710
In sha Allah.
In sha Allah, Bala Hatun.

380
00:57:07,760 --> 00:57:12,100
I want to see him and recieve his prayers.

381
00:57:14,500 --> 00:57:17,340
Also, I have something to tell him.

382
00:57:17,770 --> 00:57:20,410
Then, I'll tell you too.

383
00:57:24,620 --> 00:57:28,890
While waiting for my father,
have a seat, Osman Bey.

384
00:57:48,250 --> 00:57:52,330
- We saw your aunt Selcan.
- I know.

385
00:57:52,490 --> 00:57:54,910
I've found you thanks to her.

386
00:57:58,750 --> 00:58:02,890
I was scared that I couldn't see you
again, Bala Hatun.

387
00:58:08,850 --> 00:58:14,730
I'll send my Selcan aunt to your father,
to ask for our marriage.

388
00:58:23,510 --> 00:58:25,570
What's wrong?

389
00:58:41,410 --> 00:58:44,600
- Peace be with you.
- Peace be with you, Akça Dervish.

390
00:58:44,600 --> 00:58:47,460
- Welcome, Osman Bey.
- Thank you.

391
00:58:48,100 --> 00:58:50,720
I want to see Edebali.

392
00:58:51,760 --> 00:58:55,270
He is not available, Osman Bey.

393
00:59:03,440 --> 00:59:07,220
- Does he know that it is important?
- Yes.

394
00:59:16,560 --> 00:59:20,850
- I'll see him myself.
- Osman Bey!

395
00:59:28,150 --> 00:59:30,540
Be patient.

396
00:59:34,030 --> 00:59:38,000
Patience solves every problem.

397
00:59:38,000 --> 01:00:16,500
www.kurulusosman.online

398
01:00:17,060 --> 01:00:21,560
Your father turned me away, Bala Hatun.

399
01:00:24,120 --> 01:00:29,640
Now, are you angry with my father because
he turned you away?

400
01:00:30,770 --> 01:00:35,430
Or do you angry with yourself, who raised
his hand to an unreachable position?

401
01:00:36,470 --> 01:00:39,250
I did this to myself.

402
01:00:40,450 --> 01:00:43,670
A little problem may bother you.

403
01:00:46,980 --> 01:00:50,640
But, even big problems have their
solutions.

404
01:00:50,640 --> 01:00:53,420
I can't surrender, Bala Hatun.

405
01:00:53,550 --> 01:00:57,240
Then, you need to be patient.

406
01:01:12,660 --> 01:01:15,510
- Do you like our pot of secrets, Akça?

407
01:01:15,510 --> 01:01:19,960
It leaks water, sir.

408
01:01:19,960 --> 01:01:22,930
Then, we need to flame it.

409
01:01:23,590 --> 01:01:26,820
My father knows something for sure,
Osman Bey

410
01:01:27,880 --> 01:01:33,120
I know, being patient is hard.

411
01:01:34,390 --> 01:01:41,450
I can wait until my last breath.

412
01:01:43,420 --> 01:01:46,790
As long as I know that you can wait too.

413
01:01:49,120 --> 01:01:52,140
I can be your friend in my father's way.

414
01:01:53,180 --> 01:01:56,950
I can wait until my last breath for this
cause.

415
01:01:57,780 --> 01:02:01,210
However, know that this will be hard.

416
01:02:01,210 --> 01:02:06,120
Be my hope if I go hopeless.

417
01:02:08,490 --> 01:02:13,980
I just need to know that you will be mine.

418
01:02:17,050 --> 01:02:19,960
Do not doubt.

419
01:02:21,540 --> 01:02:26,420
I can be yours until the end of my life.

420
01:02:30,320 --> 01:02:32,880
I will be back, Bala Hatun.

421
01:02:43,330 --> 01:02:45,860
You were going to say something to me.

422
01:02:48,450 --> 01:02:52,120
- Aygül Hatun.
- What happened to her?

423
01:02:53,720 --> 01:02:56,720
She came to me in the tent.

424
01:02:57,640 --> 01:03:02,260
She said we troubled both you and
the tent.

425
01:03:02,870 --> 01:03:05,610
She warned me.

426
01:03:08,470 --> 01:03:11,420
You don't need to go crazy, Osman Bey.

427
01:03:11,830 --> 01:03:14,860
She is from your own blood.

428
01:03:14,870 --> 01:03:17,010
It is not her business.

429
01:03:17,220 --> 01:03:20,050
It's not about you or me, Osman Bey.

430
01:03:22,100 --> 01:03:24,450
What is it about, then?

431
01:03:25,600 --> 01:03:28,900
Aygül Hatun likes you.

432
01:03:30,890 --> 01:03:34,330
I know that my heart belongs to you,
Bala Hatun.

433
01:03:34,530 --> 01:03:37,310
Leave Aygül to me.

434
01:03:38,440 --> 01:03:45,470
However, I didn't know I upset Edebali
so much that he didn't want to see me.

435
01:03:47,960 --> 01:03:50,400
I will wait patiently.

436
01:03:51,800 --> 01:03:54,070
I am leaving, Bala Hatun.

437
01:04:10,570 --> 01:04:13,320
Your Efendi isn't available, Osman Bey.

438
01:04:14,040 --> 01:04:18,040
Be patient. Patience is the door to the
ultimate union, you know.

439
01:05:01,580 --> 01:05:05,130
Come here. Sit.
Come.

440
01:05:11,720 --> 01:05:14,710
Your father has something
to talk to you, daughter.

441
01:05:15,580 --> 01:05:17,490
Listen carefully.

442
01:05:20,010 --> 01:05:20,900
My daughter...

443
01:05:22,300 --> 01:05:24,400
in our traditions...

444
01:05:25,180 --> 01:05:27,440
having a daughter is precious.

445
01:05:27,910 --> 01:05:31,910
Because she is a guest who leaves
when the time comes.

446
01:05:33,530 --> 01:05:36,110
And your time has come, daughter.

447
01:05:37,350 --> 01:05:40,610
I want you to settle in a smooth place...

448
01:05:40,880 --> 01:05:43,190
... not in a brow.

449
01:05:46,660 --> 01:05:50,470
I want you to marry a man
who knows your worth.

450
01:05:53,580 --> 01:05:55,010
Today...

451
01:05:56,220 --> 01:05:58,920
I was with Alişar Bey in Kulucahisar.

452
01:06:01,050 --> 01:06:04,380
He lost his wife, you know.

453
01:06:06,060 --> 01:06:09,360
He wants you as his wife.

454
01:06:12,440 --> 01:06:14,470
He asked me about it...

455
01:06:15,620 --> 01:06:19,620
... and I'm asking you, daughter. Do you
have consent?

456
01:06:27,680 --> 01:06:29,920
Your father is asking you.

457
01:06:40,870 --> 01:06:43,090
Whatever you like, father.

458
01:06:54,800 --> 01:06:56,250
Daughter...

459
01:07:00,560 --> 01:07:04,560
... you look so confused.

460
01:07:05,170 --> 01:07:09,170
Be on your own for a while.

461
01:07:10,130 --> 01:07:12,300
Think properly.

462
01:07:13,570 --> 01:07:14,600
Okay.

463
01:07:35,170 --> 01:07:37,490
Girls can't think straight, Dündar Bey.

464
01:07:40,180 --> 01:07:43,520
You can't leave her alone with such
an important decision.

465
01:07:48,870 --> 01:07:51,560
Consent is very important!

466
01:07:52,630 --> 01:07:56,220
My daughter isn't for sale in New Bazaar!

467
01:07:58,240 --> 01:08:02,240
Let her decide on her own.

468
01:08:22,660 --> 01:08:25,400
Look at the fires of the candles, Kalanoz.

469
01:08:29,400 --> 01:08:32,460
They're so timid, they're shaking.

470
01:08:34,920 --> 01:08:37,270
They'll go out if I blow.

471
01:08:50,070 --> 01:08:52,960
Our dreams will come true, darling.

472
01:08:54,790 --> 01:08:57,820
We'll defeat Turks together.

473
01:08:59,690 --> 01:09:02,710
Master Yannis will show us the way.

474
01:09:02,830 --> 01:09:06,570
We'll walk together in that way.

475
01:09:11,430 --> 01:09:13,540
As long as you look at me like this...

476
01:09:14,880 --> 01:09:17,920
... as long as there's a fire of love
in our hearts...

477
01:09:19,460 --> 01:09:22,090
... we can do everything.

478
01:09:29,400 --> 01:09:31,180
Why is she here?

479
01:09:31,690 --> 01:09:34,840
They have migrated. They'll
settle in the tent.

480
01:09:36,910 --> 01:09:40,910
50 tents equals 500 people, Hatun.

481
01:09:41,120 --> 01:09:44,790
We can't afford anything these days.

482
01:09:44,810 --> 01:09:48,620
And now here they are.

483
01:09:48,980 --> 01:09:50,800
She asked about Osman.

484
01:09:50,880 --> 01:09:53,950
There's no need to mention Selcan Hatun.

485
01:09:54,240 --> 01:09:56,680
Keep your eyes on her.

486
01:10:15,350 --> 01:10:17,080
Welcome, aunt.

487
01:10:20,760 --> 01:10:22,760
Thanks, Dündar Bey.

488
01:10:24,470 --> 01:10:28,080
Come. It's all for you.

489
01:10:28,740 --> 01:10:30,350
Thank you.

490
01:10:47,690 --> 01:10:52,690
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

491
01:11:01,550 --> 01:11:04,030
Brother fought with his brother...

492
01:11:04,430 --> 01:11:06,840
... and the idiot believed it.

493
01:11:10,400 --> 01:11:12,280
Batur...

494
01:11:13,360 --> 01:11:15,200
Osman...

495
01:11:16,340 --> 01:11:19,240
Tell me. Is this true?

496
01:11:19,840 --> 01:11:22,740
Is there a sibling fight in our tent?

497
01:11:24,770 --> 01:11:27,810
No, aunt.
You are right.

498
01:11:28,680 --> 01:11:33,320
But, Osman adjudicated without my
permission.

499
01:11:33,950 --> 01:11:35,660
My Batur.

500
01:11:35,750 --> 01:11:37,570
My Valiant.

501
01:11:37,870 --> 01:11:39,920
Let's ask Osman.

502
01:11:40,090 --> 01:11:43,550
Aunt, let's drop this subject.

503
01:11:43,680 --> 01:11:46,040
Let's keep it cool.

504
01:11:46,650 --> 01:11:49,600
My Gündüz.
My sunlight.

505
01:11:49,670 --> 01:11:53,260
We can only solve this problem by
going after it.

506
01:11:53,620 --> 01:11:55,800
Not by escaping it.

507
01:12:01,400 --> 01:12:05,030
This case is so new, Selcan Hatun.

508
01:12:05,040 --> 01:12:07,230
If we push it, it'll be worse.

509
01:12:07,560 --> 01:12:10,270
You mustn't push it.

510
01:12:12,770 --> 01:12:17,330
We have been taught by Mother Hayma,
Söhre Hatun.

511
01:12:18,040 --> 01:12:21,870
I've lived through three Bey's reign.

512
01:12:22,020 --> 01:12:25,370
My intention is not to push.

513
01:12:25,370 --> 01:12:28,040
I want to find a solution.

514
01:12:32,340 --> 01:12:35,840
Osman, tell me.

515
01:12:35,840 --> 01:12:38,350
Is Batur right?

516
01:12:42,060 --> 01:12:45,730
He hit me when I least expected it.

517
01:12:46,140 --> 01:12:48,770
I didn't expect this from Osman.

518
01:12:51,840 --> 01:12:53,920
My Osman.

519
01:12:54,650 --> 01:12:57,970
Is what Batur says right?

520
01:13:00,460 --> 01:13:02,890
Little Osman.

521
01:13:02,910 --> 01:13:04,950
Young Osman.

522
01:13:04,970 --> 01:13:09,590
Patience is the key.

523
01:13:10,040 --> 01:13:12,370
Know this very well.

524
01:13:16,610 --> 01:13:19,030
Yes, aunt.

525
01:13:28,440 --> 01:13:30,810
He is not flawless.

526
01:13:31,520 --> 01:13:35,870
But, I acted impulsively.

527
01:13:48,170 --> 01:13:50,070
Osman..

528
01:13:51,940 --> 01:13:55,020
My dark-eyed valiant.

529
01:13:55,450 --> 01:14:00,420
Strangers spoil the brotherhood.

530
01:14:02,490 --> 01:14:08,770
I left a son and my valiant Gündoğdu
behind.

531
01:14:10,030 --> 01:14:15,180
I have no one else to trust but you.

532
01:14:16,610 --> 01:14:21,660
If you divide, how can I stand?

533
01:14:24,220 --> 01:14:28,750
This is my grandfather Korkut's
bequest.

534
01:14:28,810 --> 01:14:34,350
The ignoble tries to disunite brothers,
while the decent tries to unite.

535
01:14:37,240 --> 01:14:40,690
Come on, hug each other.

536
01:14:44,330 --> 01:14:47,150
Let this lament end.

537
01:14:47,700 --> 01:14:51,630
Let's turn the bad smell in the air into
a sweet smell.

538
01:15:11,060 --> 01:15:12,980
Give me your blessings.

539
01:15:13,370 --> 01:15:17,800
I do.
Give me your blessings.

540
01:15:18,970 --> 01:15:21,110
Hay Masha Allah (may Allah protect it.)

541
01:15:42,550 --> 01:15:46,630
Aunt, you brought your compassion.
Bless you.

542
01:15:46,710 --> 01:15:50,830
Your tent needs a mother.

543
01:15:50,910 --> 01:15:54,150
A mother's compassion.

544
01:16:24,610 --> 01:16:26,550
Daughter.

545
01:16:26,770 --> 01:16:29,070
I see you are rather silent.

546
01:16:30,730 --> 01:16:33,040
Come here.

547
01:16:50,130 --> 01:16:52,490
I hope nothing is wrong, in sha Allah.

548
01:16:52,730 --> 01:16:56,120
I am fine, father.
I am fine, but...

549
01:16:56,130 --> 01:16:58,000
... something bothers me.

550
01:16:58,950 --> 01:17:04,400
Tell me what bothers my sunshine.

551
01:17:05,290 --> 01:17:09,940
Our situation, father.
We face injustice everywhere we go.

552
01:17:10,670 --> 01:17:14,100
They set traps for us.

553
01:17:14,100 --> 01:17:20,170
How can we achieve the comfort?
This question bothers me.

554
01:17:20,900 --> 01:17:24,520
Your decedent Mother Ulduz Hatun
was just like you.

555
01:17:25,030 --> 01:17:33,190
When something bothered her, she would
sit in a corner and think all day long.

556
01:17:34,040 --> 01:17:36,940
My daughter, my Bala.

557
01:17:38,580 --> 01:17:42,980
Your heart is bothered, not you.

558
01:17:43,670 --> 01:17:48,830
A person is full of blood.

559
01:17:49,380 --> 01:17:52,540
But his heart manages him.

560
01:17:53,160 --> 01:17:57,920
Body is a nacre, heart is a pearl.

561
01:17:57,950 --> 01:18:03,240
Skin is an envelope,
heart is a letter.

562
01:18:03,600 --> 01:18:09,170
The heart is the capital of a huge
country, daughter.

563
01:18:09,220 --> 01:18:15,580
It is like a herbalist, who includes
all the cures.

564
01:18:16,340 --> 01:18:21,210
If you find the justice in your heart,
you will arrive at the land of goodness.

565
01:18:21,210 --> 01:18:26,680
If you find wisdom in your heart,
you'll arrive at the land of philosophy.

566
01:18:27,280 --> 01:18:31,890
If you find compassion in your heart,
you'll arrive at the land of mercy.

567
01:18:34,330 --> 01:18:40,010
If you find love in your heart, you'll
arrive at the land of servitude.

568
01:18:41,810 --> 01:18:47,410
As our prophet ordered...

569
01:18:48,320 --> 01:18:52,930
If our heart is strong,
all of our works will be successful.

570
01:18:55,800 --> 01:19:00,470
However, this shouldn't bother you.

571
01:19:04,040 --> 01:19:10,070
Since when have you been bothering
yourself for us, for yourself, Bala Hatun?

572
01:19:12,300 --> 01:19:18,420
If you think of yourself, you'll have
a lot of troubles.

573
01:19:19,160 --> 01:19:23,480
A person always have problems.

574
01:19:24,180 --> 01:19:27,670
A person is made of his problems.

575
01:19:30,160 --> 01:19:35,070
In the Islam world, our trouble is so
small...

576
01:19:35,160 --> 01:19:38,780
when compared to the oppresseds' troubles.

577
01:19:38,780 --> 01:19:43,400
If you're bothered with all the
humanity's troubles someday...

578
01:19:43,430 --> 01:19:47,430
that day will be our salvation Inshaallah.

579
01:19:50,270 --> 01:19:52,060
May Allah...

580
01:19:52,450 --> 01:19:55,320
... make clear all of our hearts.

581
01:19:55,600 --> 01:19:59,480
May Allah make our trouble big.

582
01:20:00,730 --> 01:20:05,830
So that the devil can't
pervade our heart.

583
01:20:06,490 --> 01:20:10,490
So that our heart will always be clean.

584
01:20:11,440 --> 01:20:12,760
Amin.

585
01:20:23,180 --> 01:20:26,520
Don't ever talk!

586
01:20:26,570 --> 01:20:28,040
Don't!

587
01:20:29,820 --> 01:20:32,470
I'll start with your fingers...

588
01:21:04,260 --> 01:21:08,260
Then I'll cut your eyelids!

589
01:21:09,050 --> 01:21:11,920
Stop, brother. Stop.

590
01:21:12,160 --> 01:21:13,430
Let me go.

591
01:21:13,480 --> 01:21:17,420
- Stop, brother.
- Let me go!

592
01:21:19,530 --> 01:21:23,530
Okay, okay! Okay! I'll tell you!

593
01:21:25,700 --> 01:21:29,080
Tell us! Tell us so you can die easily.

594
01:21:29,180 --> 01:21:31,080
I'll tell everything!

595
01:21:31,350 --> 01:21:33,630
But don't make him touch me.

596
01:21:34,440 --> 01:21:37,370
Salvador will raid Samsa's tent tomorrow.

597
01:21:38,570 --> 01:21:41,090
He'll meet his men in Caravanserai.

598
01:21:48,260 --> 01:21:49,390
Tell me...

599
01:21:49,410 --> 01:21:51,540
How will we recognize him?

600
01:21:51,860 --> 01:21:55,430
There's a big sign behind his head.

601
01:22:09,680 --> 01:22:12,470
Wait here, brother.

602
01:22:12,800 --> 01:22:15,250
I'll inform our Bey.

603
01:22:15,560 --> 01:22:16,810
Come on!

604
01:22:22,130 --> 01:22:26,980
I still remember the day
My Ertuğrul Bey...

605
01:22:27,140 --> 01:22:29,480
... brought your late mother to the tent.

606
01:22:32,840 --> 01:22:35,420
They survived so many hardships.

607
01:22:38,230 --> 01:22:41,100
So many bad things happened to...

608
01:22:41,100 --> 01:22:45,100
... your mother and father just because
she came to the tent.

609
01:22:50,950 --> 01:22:53,500
May Allah rest my Halime.

610
01:22:57,740 --> 01:23:01,170
She stood up to everyone and everything.

611
01:23:01,970 --> 01:23:03,450
Even to me.

612
01:23:11,270 --> 01:23:14,010
She said that you'd follow your father.

613
01:23:15,110 --> 01:23:17,460
She was right.

614
01:23:18,210 --> 01:23:24,340
You'll deal with the men of the
devil named Yannis.

615
01:23:24,990 --> 01:23:27,460
Don't worry, aunt.

616
01:23:27,670 --> 01:23:31,670
I'll deal with that devil.

617
01:23:32,330 --> 01:23:33,890
I know.

618
01:23:40,800 --> 01:23:42,160
Tell me...

619
01:23:43,150 --> 01:23:45,560
... what do you wish?

620
01:23:52,500 --> 01:23:55,080
I love Bala Hatun, aunt.

621
01:24:00,320 --> 01:24:03,080
I can tell from your eyes, son.

622
01:24:03,610 --> 01:24:07,910
Even when you say her
name, your eyes glow.

623
01:24:11,080 --> 01:24:12,100
Tell me...

624
01:24:12,740 --> 01:24:14,780
... what do you want?

625
01:24:15,740 --> 01:24:18,530
I want you to go to Edebalı's place
tomorrow.

626
01:24:21,000 --> 01:24:22,510
My Osman...

627
01:24:24,680 --> 01:24:26,860
With Allah's order...

628
01:24:27,730 --> 01:24:30,900
I want you to ask for (marriage)
Bala Hatun, aunt.

629
01:24:33,520 --> 01:24:36,370
Thank Allah, we've seen these days.

630
01:24:40,490 --> 01:24:44,010
Why do you send me when
there's your father?

631
01:24:44,050 --> 01:24:46,590
He has a long way to go, aunt.

632
01:24:47,510 --> 01:24:50,280
I don't know when he'll return.

633
01:24:51,140 --> 01:24:52,400
And...

634
01:24:55,330 --> 01:24:57,700
I'm out of patience.

635
01:24:59,270 --> 01:25:01,410
We'll hold the wedding
when my father comes.

636
01:25:03,790 --> 01:25:05,200
And...

637
01:25:07,680 --> 01:25:10,590
I broke Edebalı's heart.

638
01:25:10,750 --> 01:25:13,870
I did some bad things.

639
01:25:14,500 --> 01:25:16,400
He warned me.

640
01:25:17,320 --> 01:25:18,540
But...

641
01:25:19,270 --> 01:25:21,550
... it was too late, aunt.

642
01:25:21,910 --> 01:25:23,320
Your uncle...

643
01:25:23,950 --> 01:25:27,950
Should I ask for Bala Hatun
when there's your uncle?

644
01:25:28,840 --> 01:25:30,130
My uncle...

645
01:25:31,650 --> 01:25:33,730
... is half my father, aunt.

646
01:25:35,570 --> 01:25:36,970
But...

647
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:42,300
... you're my mother.

648
01:25:42,440 --> 01:25:45,020
I'd die for you.

649
01:25:46,200 --> 01:25:48,180
I don't need Dündar Bey...

650
01:25:49,120 --> 01:25:51,530
when my mother is here.

651
01:25:53,330 --> 01:25:55,280
Don't worry...

652
01:25:55,280 --> 01:25:59,150
I'll visit that holy man Edebalı tomorrow.

653
01:26:01,260 --> 01:26:02,890
Thanks, aunt.

654
01:26:04,900 --> 01:26:07,100
And there's one more problem, aunt.

655
01:26:07,270 --> 01:26:08,950
Tell me.

656
01:26:09,850 --> 01:26:11,380
Aygül.

657
01:26:36,010 --> 01:26:40,010
Your father closed the door
to his guest, Bala Hatun.

658
01:26:57,850 --> 01:27:02,390
Love and compassion is like a
river inside a person.

659
01:27:03,480 --> 01:27:07,480
If it flows strong, the evil
can't hold it.

660
01:27:11,500 --> 01:27:13,340
Osman Bey...

661
01:27:13,410 --> 01:27:16,030
... babbles like a river.

662
01:27:17,540 --> 01:27:21,540
His love and compassion are
strong, thank Allah.

663
01:27:22,530 --> 01:27:23,790
But...

664
01:27:24,200 --> 01:27:26,160
... he's so cruel.

665
01:27:27,260 --> 01:27:28,820
And overhasty.

666
01:27:29,600 --> 01:27:31,120
And wrathful.

667
01:27:32,580 --> 01:27:34,560
He said he would be with you...

668
01:27:35,300 --> 01:27:38,230
... until his last breath.

669
01:27:39,750 --> 01:27:42,020
Don't you believe him?

670
01:27:42,130 --> 01:27:44,610
I do, but...

671
01:27:45,450 --> 01:27:47,160
Then what?

672
01:27:53,370 --> 01:27:56,740
My father left Osman in a hard position.

673
01:27:57,530 --> 01:27:59,790
I am scared of the fact that...

674
01:27:59,880 --> 01:28:02,700
... he may struggle too much.

675
01:28:31,160 --> 01:28:34,600
Osman Bey.
Be patient.

676
01:28:34,710 --> 01:28:38,380
Patience solves every problem.

677
01:28:49,220 --> 01:28:51,630
Osman...

678
01:28:51,630 --> 01:28:56,880
Osman, who goes high suddenly, then
goes low immediately...

679
01:28:57,300 --> 01:28:59,280
Little Osman.

680
01:28:59,430 --> 01:29:04,160
We tell you to be fair...

681
01:29:04,350 --> 01:29:08,110
We tell you to be merciful...

682
01:29:08,250 --> 01:29:12,920
We tell you to stand against cruelty...

683
01:29:13,090 --> 01:29:17,890
And may people see the state in you...

684
01:29:17,970 --> 01:29:20,130
But, look at what you have done.

685
01:29:20,250 --> 01:29:22,560
Little Osman.

686
01:29:22,910 --> 01:29:24,750
Young Osman.

687
01:29:24,750 --> 01:29:29,560
Patience is the key.

688
01:29:42,910 --> 01:29:45,230
Can I come in, my Bey?

689
01:29:47,020 --> 01:29:49,280
Come.

690
01:29:52,910 --> 01:29:54,480
Boran.

691
01:29:55,350 --> 01:29:57,560
What are you doing here?

692
01:29:58,010 --> 01:30:01,460
- Where is Kanturalı?
- I left him, my Bey.

693
01:30:01,460 --> 01:30:04,600
Why?
Why are you here?

694
01:30:04,600 --> 01:30:06,700
Hoan spoke, my Bey.

695
01:30:06,700 --> 01:30:10,050
Salvador will raid Samsa Bey's tent.

696
01:30:10,050 --> 01:30:13,330
- We can't leave you alone.
- Damn faithless'!

697
01:30:13,330 --> 01:30:15,310
They will raid Sergeant Samsa, ha?

698
01:30:15,310 --> 01:30:19,650
I will rip their hearts off and let the
dogs eat them!

699
01:30:20,010 --> 01:30:24,390
My Alps, let's go to Sergeant Samsa's
tent.

700
01:30:25,000 --> 01:30:27,810
We will make them pay!

701
01:30:27,890 --> 01:30:29,940
Eyvallah, (Okay) my Bey.

702
01:31:01,250 --> 01:31:04,040
As years pass...

703
01:31:04,380 --> 01:31:09,240
... Kayı tent has changed, Aybüke.

704
01:31:10,790 --> 01:31:15,080
It has gotten old, and it has gotten
bigger.

705
01:31:15,250 --> 01:31:18,080
And it has gotten more troubles.

706
01:31:18,110 --> 01:31:20,970
We are in the middle of those troubles,
my Hanım (lady).

707
01:31:21,150 --> 01:31:24,390
We came up to a complicated time.

708
01:31:25,150 --> 01:31:27,260
What does bother you?

709
01:31:27,540 --> 01:31:29,580
Zöhre Hatun.

710
01:31:29,660 --> 01:31:31,990
I guess she is not so happy to see us.

711
01:31:31,990 --> 01:31:33,980
Why would she be happy?

712
01:31:34,010 --> 01:31:39,400
She set a brother against another.

713
01:31:43,460 --> 01:31:46,620
They left my Osman alone.

714
01:31:46,680 --> 01:31:52,270
She knows that I love him as my son.
She is anxious because I am here now.

715
01:31:52,270 --> 01:31:55,320
Zöhre Hatun bears a grudge.

716
01:31:55,320 --> 01:31:57,580
I hope she doesn't hurt you.

717
01:31:58,350 --> 01:32:02,170
What Zöhre Hatun knows is only Dündar
Bey's bed.

718
01:32:02,460 --> 01:32:06,460
I experienced three ages, and three huge
migration.

719
01:32:08,520 --> 01:32:11,870
Look at the color of this hair.

720
01:32:11,950 --> 01:32:16,770
She only makes herself listened to the
young ones.

721
01:32:16,770 --> 01:32:19,210
She cannot command me.

722
01:32:30,360 --> 01:32:32,830
Archers!

723
01:32:33,010 --> 01:32:35,380
Shoot me.

724
01:33:57,600 --> 01:34:02,800
You can be martyred at any time.

725
01:34:05,040 --> 01:34:09,860
I don't accept any faults!
Know that very well!

726
01:34:16,990 --> 01:34:21,940
We've raided infidel cities for a war.

727
01:34:22,900 --> 01:34:25,800
The regulation has changed!

728
01:34:26,350 --> 01:34:31,620
From now on, we will protect our land,
our honor, our tent!

729
01:34:34,760 --> 01:34:40,030
The Beys in the Turkish tents act
carelessly!

730
01:34:43,480 --> 01:34:47,430
You will fight, you will kill
the infidel!

731
01:34:47,580 --> 01:34:54,870
Don't come to me without killing ten
infidels before being martyred!

732
01:34:56,500 --> 01:34:59,730
I will chase you in the next world!

733
01:34:59,920 --> 01:35:03,530
- Understood?
- Yes, my Bey!

734
01:35:13,950 --> 01:35:16,660
Everyone knows what to do!

735
01:35:17,050 --> 01:35:23,040
The genie is out of the bottle!

736
01:35:23,140 --> 01:35:25,850
We will end this today!

737
01:35:26,030 --> 01:35:30,010
We have just a single
arrow in the quiver!

738
01:35:30,150 --> 01:35:36,130
This is our only chance!
If we fail...

739
01:35:36,170 --> 01:35:40,480
We may not sleep at nights from now on.

740
01:35:40,590 --> 01:35:42,340
Do you understand me?

741
01:36:02,900 --> 01:36:06,970
Yes, Selcan Hatun?
Is there something important?

742
01:36:09,150 --> 01:36:12,700
I came to talk about Aygül Hatun.

743
01:36:12,710 --> 01:36:16,120
I will cut it short.

744
01:36:16,140 --> 01:36:18,480
Do you not cut it short normally?

745
01:36:18,480 --> 01:36:20,270
No.

746
01:36:20,600 --> 01:36:22,240
What happened to my daughter?

747
01:36:22,250 --> 01:36:25,850
I know Aygül likes Osman.

748
01:36:25,980 --> 01:36:28,100
Who told you that?

749
01:36:28,100 --> 01:36:32,080
I see it in your eyes. So it's true.

750
01:36:32,120 --> 01:36:36,730
Tell me what do you want to say.

751
01:36:37,370 --> 01:36:41,330
Osman loves another Hatun, Zöhre.

752
01:36:42,540 --> 01:36:47,440
Both I and my daughter know that Osman
likes Edebalı's daughter.

753
01:36:47,510 --> 01:36:51,170
What does this have to do with me or
my daughter?

754
01:36:51,170 --> 01:36:56,210
If so, why did Aygül threaten Bala Hatun?

755
01:36:56,510 --> 01:37:01,210
She says "we don't want you here, you
draw our tent into trouble."

756
01:37:02,030 --> 01:37:06,980
My daughter is right.
But, not because she likes Osman.

757
01:37:06,980 --> 01:37:12,450
Because she knows both that Hatun
and her father will trouble our tent.

758
01:37:12,450 --> 01:37:17,350
Also, Aygül likes Alişer Bey.

759
01:37:17,360 --> 01:37:22,880
Alişer Bey asked for my daughter's hand
from Dündar Bey, by the grace of Allah.

760
01:37:24,070 --> 01:37:26,930
This conversation is over.

761
01:37:27,590 --> 01:37:32,520
I am happy about this.
May Allah make them happy, in sha Allah.

762
01:37:32,800 --> 01:37:34,470
Amin.

763
01:37:34,520 --> 01:37:37,750
Obviously, there are things to do in
this tent, Zöhre.

764
01:37:37,750 --> 01:37:40,530
I'll go back to my things.

765
01:38:33,420 --> 01:38:36,420
I've heard you were
looking for me, Osman Bey.

766
01:38:39,610 --> 01:38:43,610
You are looking for the killer
of Aybars, who I slaughtered.

767
01:38:45,050 --> 01:38:47,190
Well then, here I am.

768
01:38:47,970 --> 01:38:49,940
Salvador.

769
01:38:50,430 --> 01:38:54,210
Come, let us solve this as men do.

770
01:38:54,410 --> 01:38:58,410
When did you come and
confront me as a man, Salvador?

771
01:38:58,640 --> 01:39:01,070
Are you brave with your
sword, or your tongue?

772
01:39:01,300 --> 01:39:06,750
You took so many of my men's lifes for just one of
your Alps, did you really think I would forget that?

773
01:39:07,770 --> 01:39:10,110
Now you are in my hands.

774
01:39:10,590 --> 01:39:15,830
Our fire of vengeance doesn't extinguish
until the soil has enough blood.

775
01:39:16,450 --> 01:39:20,450
I won't kill you until you have
enough of your own casualties!

776
01:39:21,430 --> 01:39:23,720
- Allah is Great!
- Allah is one!

777
01:39:23,720 --> 01:39:24,540
Attack!

778
01:40:22,060 --> 01:40:22,850
Alps.

779
01:40:45,090 --> 01:40:46,480
Erkut!

780
01:41:15,470 --> 01:41:17,330
Erkut! Brother!

781
01:41:17,370 --> 01:41:20,870
Drop your sword if you don't
want your Alps to die, Osman!

782
01:41:21,750 --> 01:41:24,830
I won't tell you again!

783
01:41:26,890 --> 01:41:29,830
My Bey. Don't!

784
01:41:43,870 --> 01:41:46,190
Erkut! Erkut!

785
01:43:11,360 --> 01:43:13,220
You called me, mother.

786
01:43:14,110 --> 01:43:18,960
Come, daughter, sit.
I need to talk to you.

787
01:43:24,440 --> 01:43:28,000
I wanted to talk to
you about Alişar Bey.

788
01:43:28,770 --> 01:43:33,970
Your father won't give you to him
without your consent, you know that too.

789
01:43:37,550 --> 01:43:42,240
But you have to marry Alişar Bey, Aygül.

790
01:43:50,020 --> 01:43:58,490
The future of your father, us, our Tent,
and even your brother depends on it.

791
01:43:58,880 --> 01:44:01,930
What are you saying,
mother? What future?

792
01:44:03,220 --> 01:44:07,480
- Your father's future of Beyhood, daughter.
- Mother, do you hear your words?

793
01:44:08,460 --> 01:44:10,180
Look, daughter.

794
01:44:11,470 --> 01:44:16,460
I am a healer,
Ertuğrul Bey is sick for days.

795
01:44:17,520 --> 01:44:22,860
He's been hiding this from everyone,
I knew it too but I stayed silent.

796
01:44:23,640 --> 01:44:27,570
When the time comes, your father's
chance for Beyhood will be clear.

797
01:44:28,090 --> 01:44:30,590
What does it have to do with me, mother?

798
01:44:30,700 --> 01:44:33,600
Don't you know how vindictive Osman is?

799
01:44:34,230 --> 01:44:39,110
After all that happened, Osman will neither
forgive your father nor your brother.

800
01:44:42,570 --> 01:44:47,300
If your father doesn't become Bey,
eventually, Osman will be.

801
01:44:47,700 --> 01:44:50,350
No one could prevent that from happening.

802
01:44:51,620 --> 01:44:54,070
Except for Alişar Bey.

803
01:44:54,990 --> 01:44:56,930
Did you understand me?

804
01:45:07,580 --> 01:45:10,270
I've arranged a feast of
blood for you, Osman.

805
01:45:13,270 --> 01:45:15,890
Even death won't save you from me!

806
01:45:51,820 --> 01:45:55,750
No, no!

807
01:46:06,950 --> 01:46:11,870
- Where is Edebali?
- Osman Bey, don't you tell a thing to this infidel!

808
01:46:11,990 --> 01:46:15,420
- Demirbüken!
- I would give my life for you.

809
01:46:15,540 --> 01:46:19,540
- Demirbüken!
- This is such an emotional scene.

810
01:46:20,280 --> 01:46:24,690
- I bear witness that there is no god but Allah...
- No!

811
01:46:25,170 --> 01:46:29,530
... and I bear witness that Muhammad
is His servant and messenger.

812
01:46:30,990 --> 01:46:32,440
No!

813
01:46:56,970 --> 01:46:59,630
At the sunrise, and the sunset...

814
01:47:00,020 --> 01:47:06,360
... every moment you don't tell me where
Edebali is, I will cut one of your Alps' throats.

815
01:47:08,850 --> 01:47:10,080
We are leaving!

816
01:47:14,110 --> 01:47:17,370
Demirbüken, Demirbüken!

817
01:47:18,720 --> 01:47:20,190
Erkut!

818
01:47:55,560 --> 01:47:58,840
Water, water!

819
01:47:58,990 --> 01:48:00,570
Shut your mouth!

820
01:48:06,080 --> 01:48:08,600
I've told you everything you wanted!

821
01:48:09,780 --> 01:48:11,420
A little bit water.

822
01:48:12,660 --> 01:48:15,680
If something happens to Samsa Bey...

823
01:48:16,350 --> 01:48:18,410
... I will flay your skin!

824
01:48:19,410 --> 01:48:20,580
Water.

825
01:51:03,500 --> 01:51:09,110
Are these carpets worth putting in the
stalls of the skillful women of Kayı?

826
01:51:10,900 --> 01:51:14,840
Since when the daughters of
Hayme Hatun, Halime Hatun...

827
01:51:15,150 --> 01:51:19,150
...have left weaving and
started working with rags?

828
01:51:27,520 --> 01:51:33,050
We would sit on the bench at
sunrise, and leave with the sunset.

829
01:51:33,320 --> 01:51:37,320
We would treat our fingers
with balsam pear...

830
01:51:37,480 --> 01:51:39,430
... to stop the pain.

831
01:51:40,320 --> 01:51:42,500
Go and continue your work.

832
01:51:45,450 --> 01:51:53,000
Tell me, Zöhre Hatun, have I spoken too much?
Do you think these carpets are worthy of Kayı Tent?

833
01:51:53,640 --> 01:51:58,110
You are right, but nothing
is the same as before.

834
01:51:58,210 --> 01:52:06,010
We collect the plants from Söğüt, they don't
give their colors fully even if we boil them for days.

835
01:52:07,700 --> 01:52:11,700
These are all just excuses
for your misery.

836
01:52:13,970 --> 01:52:15,370
I know.

837
01:52:16,010 --> 01:52:19,100
You are blinded by the
profits you can make.

838
01:52:20,770 --> 01:52:23,700
Hatuns, my sisters!

839
01:52:24,010 --> 01:52:27,560
Is it too hard to find rare
plants and bring them?

840
01:52:27,650 --> 01:52:31,650
Is it too hard to weave the best carpet?

841
01:52:32,020 --> 01:52:37,340
From now on, we can continue
the way that Mother Hayme left.

842
01:52:38,090 --> 01:52:44,030
I know that the girls of
Kayı Tent is very skillful.

843
01:52:44,550 --> 01:52:51,230
Now, let them see what can Kayı
Tent's girls do with their talents.

844
01:52:51,550 --> 01:53:00,300
I know, we will weave such carpets here that
even you won't look back to what you worked on before.

845
01:54:01,330 --> 01:54:05,580
We meet again, Selcan Hatun.

846
01:54:08,060 --> 01:54:12,060
Welcome, Dündar Bey is in his tent, come.

847
01:54:15,780 --> 01:54:20,420
Zöhre Hatun, we are here
to honor the peace.

848
01:54:20,710 --> 01:54:22,990
We came here as friends.

849
01:54:24,260 --> 01:54:28,930
And you wanted to see the
carpets, princess, come.

850
01:54:48,410 --> 01:54:55,420
Let's see, how strong is this Osman
Bey that people don't stop talking about.

851
01:55:05,290 --> 01:55:08,840
Free me, and we shall see that together.

852
01:55:09,780 --> 01:55:12,740
This dog doesn't
have the heart, my Bey.

853
01:55:12,740 --> 01:55:18,180
These idiots can only kidnap Hatuns
from the marketplace for gold.

854
01:55:18,860 --> 01:55:22,820
Then they walk the
lands as brave warriors.

855
01:55:23,020 --> 01:55:25,150
Enough of this trash talk!

856
01:55:25,380 --> 01:55:27,430
Tell us your price and we will buy you...

857
01:55:28,770 --> 01:55:31,130
... like the dog you are!

858
01:55:34,240 --> 01:55:35,270
My Bey!

859
01:55:38,520 --> 01:55:40,180
Osman Bey!

860
01:55:55,140 --> 01:55:56,750
You are a dog!

861
01:55:57,020 --> 01:55:58,680
Your turn will come too!

862
01:56:00,500 --> 01:56:02,050
Don't worry.

863
01:56:09,030 --> 01:56:10,800
Where is Edebali?

864
01:56:13,090 --> 01:56:14,690
Where is Edebali?

865
01:56:15,290 --> 01:56:17,210
He's in the place
that you will die!

866
01:56:31,790 --> 01:56:32,630
My Bey!

867
01:56:34,770 --> 01:56:36,090
Allah is Great!

868
01:56:37,540 --> 01:56:38,620
My Bey!

869
01:57:10,810 --> 01:57:12,230
Osman Bey!

870
01:57:12,690 --> 01:57:14,440
Where is Edebali?

871
01:57:36,180 --> 01:57:38,090
Where is Edebali?

872
01:57:40,840 --> 01:57:42,460
Where is Edebali?

873
01:58:27,270 --> 01:58:28,900
He fell asleep.

874
02:00:19,020 --> 02:00:20,320
Father?

875
02:00:26,630 --> 02:00:28,610
Are you alright, Inshallah?

876
02:00:33,240 --> 02:00:36,480
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

877
02:00:41,280 --> 02:00:42,590
Osman.

878
02:00:48,220 --> 02:00:50,240
What happened to Osman, father?

879
02:00:53,400 --> 02:00:56,430
Send word to dervishes, daughter.

880
02:00:57,260 --> 02:00:59,920
Tell them to check the forest carefully.

881
02:01:49,650 --> 02:01:51,680
That horse...

882
02:01:55,120 --> 02:01:57,860
What are you up to again, Osman?

883
02:02:30,090 --> 02:02:32,040
Who are you?

884
02:02:34,670 --> 02:02:38,670
I have an important
offer for you, Dündar Bey.

885
02:02:40,630 --> 02:02:42,160
Tell me about it.

886
02:02:43,150 --> 02:02:45,330
Alişar Bey is ambitious.

887
02:02:46,080 --> 02:02:50,080
But we can do greater things together.

888
02:02:55,270 --> 02:02:58,340
You are sailing too
close to the wind, Kalonoz.

889
02:02:58,720 --> 02:03:02,530
Don't you know that you
can't even walk in these lands...

890
02:03:02,650 --> 02:03:05,540
... without Alişar Bey's notice?

891
02:03:05,690 --> 02:03:08,620
Alişar Bey is nothing without us!

892
02:03:11,990 --> 02:03:14,440
I know that very well, Dündar Bey.

893
02:03:17,250 --> 02:03:20,120
Just get to the point, Kalonoz.

894
02:03:20,800 --> 02:03:23,990
Marketplaces are not
just in Söğüt or Eskihisar.

895
02:03:24,820 --> 02:03:29,080
There are also markeplaces in our
lands, waiting to be alive again.

896
02:03:29,770 --> 02:03:32,780
Those marketplaces are weak and poor.

897
02:03:32,940 --> 02:03:37,670
But together, we can enhance
both our income and our power...

898
02:03:38,450 --> 02:03:43,930
... by reviving the marketplaces
in the Byzantine.

899
02:03:48,930 --> 02:03:50,340
What do you say?

900
02:04:06,090 --> 02:04:09,870
Your carpets, fabrics...

901
02:04:10,300 --> 02:04:14,300
... are amongst the most sold
goods in Constantinople.

902
02:04:16,130 --> 02:04:20,510
It seems people of Constantinople know
a good carpet when they see one.

903
02:04:21,750 --> 02:04:24,630
What is your wish, Princess?

904
02:04:37,100 --> 02:04:39,700
Increase your carpets, produce more goods.

905
02:04:40,600 --> 02:04:45,960
We want to directly take them
and sell them in Constantinople.

906
02:04:47,880 --> 02:04:53,310
More carpets mean more
Hatuns, more benches.

907
02:04:53,890 --> 02:04:56,370
We are ready to provide whatever you need.

908
02:04:57,580 --> 02:05:01,580
We will do this together with
Selcan Hatun, right, Hatun?

909
02:05:01,790 --> 02:05:05,790
If you are going to live
here, gold is important.

910
02:05:07,820 --> 02:05:12,860
If it was just gold and coins, these
wouldn't be trapped in their stone castles.

911
02:05:19,300 --> 02:05:21,790
I will consider it anyway.

912
02:05:39,900 --> 02:05:42,970
Ya Allah, Ya Allah!

913
02:05:46,350 --> 02:05:47,670
Brother!

914
02:05:49,790 --> 02:05:51,500
He's alive, he's alive!

915
02:05:52,370 --> 02:05:53,790
Brother!

916
02:05:54,420 --> 02:05:55,550
Brother!

917
02:05:57,180 --> 02:05:59,220
They have Osman Bey!

918
02:06:01,180 --> 02:06:02,860
Go and tell the Tent!

919
02:06:02,950 --> 02:06:06,430
Go and inform our sir, I will
carry the wounded to the Tent!

920
02:06:07,460 --> 02:06:10,990
Okay, brother. Okay.

921
02:06:16,630 --> 02:06:18,480
Ya Allah!

922
02:06:36,420 --> 02:06:40,420
You see, your Alps care about you.

923
02:06:42,620 --> 02:06:47,330
Let's see which one
of them you care more.

924
02:07:07,070 --> 02:07:09,110
Is that this restless one?

925
02:07:32,750 --> 02:07:34,320
Coward!

926
02:07:35,780 --> 02:07:38,050
You will pay for what you did!

927
02:07:40,960 --> 02:07:42,500
Demon!

928
02:07:46,070 --> 02:07:48,040
You are a demon!

929
02:07:49,920 --> 02:07:51,570
You will die!

930
02:07:52,590 --> 02:07:56,090
Or is that this barbarian?

931
02:07:58,510 --> 02:08:01,190
He even has battle wounds on his face.

932
02:08:01,970 --> 02:08:08,830
I am sorry you will die in a pitiful way,
but Osman will decide when you will die.

933
02:08:09,230 --> 02:08:10,500
Huh, Osman?

934
02:08:11,290 --> 02:08:12,510
Tell me...

935
02:08:13,380 --> 02:08:14,420
which one?

936
02:08:21,670 --> 02:08:27,010
What I'm saying is, friends,
Yusuf's dungeon was dark.

937
02:08:27,130 --> 02:08:33,480
What turned that dark dungeon
to a beautiful garden was Yusuf's faith.

938
02:08:34,500 --> 02:08:36,440
It wasn't the well...

939
02:08:36,880 --> 02:08:42,100
... or Egypt, or the dungeon
that made Yusuf holy.

940
02:08:43,250 --> 02:08:46,080
One could need light to
escape from the well...

941
02:08:47,460 --> 02:08:50,040
... or a decree to
get out of the dungeon...

942
02:08:50,430 --> 02:08:54,780
... or wisdom to be a Sultan to Egypt.

943
02:08:55,390 --> 02:09:01,540
But faith is what one needs to
have in order to be like Yusuf.

944
02:09:02,270 --> 02:09:03,790
Amenna (We believed).

945
02:09:06,740 --> 02:09:10,120
Faith turns the future to reality...

946
02:09:10,630 --> 02:09:15,290
... far to close, and
defeated to victorious.

947
02:09:17,850 --> 02:09:20,920
May Allah makes us the ones
that are free in any way.

948
02:09:21,190 --> 02:09:22,300
Amin.

949
02:09:26,970 --> 02:09:32,730
Attack on the New Bazaar was bad
for the reputation of the region.

950
02:09:33,400 --> 02:09:41,060
But it seems that there won't be anyone
who will be there after it's reestablished but us.

951
02:09:41,450 --> 02:09:42,800
Edebali.

952
02:09:47,100 --> 02:09:49,620
There is Edebali, Dündar Bey.

953
02:09:50,050 --> 02:09:54,680
Âhi is what people think when
you talk about craft, trade.

954
02:09:55,790 --> 02:10:01,790
Âhi means trouble, Bamsı Bey,
it means big trouble for everyone.

955
02:10:02,180 --> 02:10:06,880
Neither I or Alişar Bey
can give him a place there.

956
02:10:09,740 --> 02:10:15,900
We have to take advantage of the
absence of the Âhis and other merchants.

957
02:10:16,830 --> 02:10:20,200
My nephew, you stay strong.

958
02:10:20,650 --> 02:10:25,850
People still didn't forget about it, uncle,
the blood is still fresh in the Bazaar.

959
02:10:26,350 --> 02:10:31,020
It wouldn't suit us to use the
attack for something like this.

960
02:10:32,550 --> 02:10:34,590
This is not using, my nephew.

961
02:10:35,430 --> 02:10:38,930
And do you think I am not in pain?

962
02:10:39,510 --> 02:10:44,590
Are these people going
to eat sorrow, drink tears?

963
02:10:45,810 --> 02:10:50,760
We need to reestablish the Bazaar
quickly and let people trade there.

964
02:10:51,070 --> 02:10:56,040
And everyone saw that the
marketplace that is not protected by...

965
02:10:56,350 --> 02:11:00,350
... my Kayı Alps, is
suitable for an attack.

966
02:11:00,840 --> 02:11:02,090
This will also...

967
02:11:02,870 --> 02:11:06,870
... increase our reputation in the region.

968
02:11:07,490 --> 02:11:11,310
Does Sofia agree with
this decision, Dündar Bey?

969
02:11:18,290 --> 02:11:22,960
Sofia made a promise to me
with his Commander Kalonoz.

970
02:11:23,520 --> 02:11:28,150
She will continue the way her
deceased husband Yorgopolos left.

971
02:11:28,430 --> 02:11:31,960
If only you cared about Sheyh
Edebali, coming to our lands...

972
02:11:31,970 --> 02:11:35,280
... as much as you care about
an alliance with the enemy!

973
02:11:40,750 --> 02:11:44,360
Don't forget that Mongols
took Gündoğdu Bey and his son.

974
02:11:44,550 --> 02:11:47,940
Edebali brought trouble wherever he went.

975
02:11:48,180 --> 02:11:50,720
We don't want any
more blood to be spilled.

976
02:11:51,030 --> 02:11:56,140
You shouldn't have bothered,
Zöhre Hatun, you can't escape your fate.

977
02:12:01,120 --> 02:12:04,330
I hope nothing's wrong.

978
02:12:39,670 --> 02:12:42,120
May I come in, Dündar Bey?

979
02:12:43,540 --> 02:12:47,540
- Abdurrahman!
- Father!

980
02:12:50,770 --> 02:12:52,550
Brother?

981
02:12:54,900 --> 02:12:57,160
Come inside, Abdurrahman Ghazi!

982
02:13:09,090 --> 02:13:10,900
Peace be with you.

983
02:13:10,990 --> 02:13:12,460
Peace be with you.

984
02:13:26,210 --> 02:13:28,640
Where is my brother, Abdurrahman Ghazi?

985
02:13:34,790 --> 02:13:36,750
Don't be silent, Abdurrahman Gazi.

986
02:13:38,060 --> 02:13:39,750
What is my father's condition?

987
02:13:48,090 --> 02:13:49,990
Abdurrahman Gazi.

988
02:13:51,800 --> 02:13:55,110
We went to many healers from Konya...

989
02:13:55,470 --> 02:13:57,430
... to Kayseri with my Ertuğrul Bey.

990
02:13:58,260 --> 02:14:02,260
Doctors from Gevher
Sultan Infirmary said that...

991
02:14:03,230 --> 02:14:06,990
... "the illness has
spread to his lungs...

992
02:14:07,550 --> 02:14:13,080
... he needs to be treated,
he should stay here for a while."

993
02:14:17,670 --> 02:14:21,670
- His remedy will be Allah, inshallah.
- Inshallah.

994
02:14:22,600 --> 02:14:23,670
Inshallah.

995
02:14:25,530 --> 02:14:26,810
Father.

996
02:14:36,410 --> 02:14:40,000
- Sir, may I?
- Speak, Dervish Pehlivan.

997
02:14:40,580 --> 02:14:43,860
Osman Bey and his Alps
were ambushed in the forest.

998
02:14:45,330 --> 02:14:47,060
They were taken.

999
02:14:52,080 --> 02:14:53,460
Who did this?

1000
02:14:54,760 --> 02:14:55,980
We don't know, sir.

1001
02:15:02,070 --> 02:15:04,220
Prepare my weapon.

1002
02:15:13,430 --> 02:15:14,610
Friends...

1003
02:15:15,440 --> 02:15:19,440
... this is not the day
to be a Pîr, but a soldier.

1004
02:15:22,070 --> 02:15:24,490
We won't leave Osman alone.

1005
02:15:24,760 --> 02:15:27,410
We won't stand still either, father.

1006
02:15:36,720 --> 02:15:40,960
Ertuğrul Bey thinks about his
Tent, even in his condition.

1007
02:15:42,340 --> 02:15:45,970
He's afraid that Tent's
business could be hindered.

1008
02:15:50,510 --> 02:15:53,880
This is the will of Ertuğrul Bey,
son of Süleyman Şah.

1009
02:15:55,130 --> 02:15:56,920
He said "my Brother Dündar...

1010
02:15:59,900 --> 02:16:01,820
..." will be my deputy.".

1011
02:16:09,520 --> 02:16:11,490
He said "my sons should
obey...

1012
02:16:12,860 --> 02:16:16,860
... their uncle, and my Beys
should obey their Ağa...

1013
02:16:19,010 --> 02:16:21,470
... so that everything would be easier."

1014
02:16:43,330 --> 02:16:47,330
I congratulate your Beyhood, Dündar Bey.

1015
02:17:56,110 --> 02:18:02,000
May your Beyhood be magnificent,
may your sword be sharp, My Bey.

1016
02:18:03,140 --> 02:18:05,060
I sharpened my sword...

1017
02:18:05,800 --> 02:18:10,080
... with your eyes, thank you, Hatun.

1018
02:18:10,780 --> 02:18:12,300
Thank you.

1019
02:18:22,120 --> 02:18:26,120
- I congratulate you, father.
- Thank you, daughter.

1020
02:18:32,410 --> 02:18:36,410
- May Allah help you on your way, my Bey.
- Thank you, daughter.

1021
02:18:46,650 --> 02:18:50,650
May your Beyhood be great, father.

1022
02:18:51,340 --> 02:18:53,030
Thank you, my son.

1023
02:19:12,060 --> 02:19:15,020
May Allah help you on your way, uncle.

1024
02:19:17,110 --> 02:19:19,090
My father's will.

1025
02:19:20,410 --> 02:19:24,530
I will obey you, and make your job easier.

1026
02:19:24,950 --> 02:19:28,950
My brother will come to this Tent...

1027
02:19:30,150 --> 02:19:32,320
... on his horse, safe and sound.

1028
02:19:33,700 --> 02:19:36,020
Don't be upset about it.

1029
02:20:12,170 --> 02:20:13,970
If it's...

1030
02:20:14,770 --> 02:20:16,440
... the order of...

1031
02:20:16,840 --> 02:20:18,490
... our Ertuğrul Bey...

1032
02:20:19,480 --> 02:20:24,130
... then we will obey, Dündar Bey.

1033
02:20:50,890 --> 02:20:53,110
Congratulations, Dündar Bey.

1034
02:21:16,610 --> 02:21:17,650
My brother...

1035
02:21:17,980 --> 02:21:19,670
May I come in, my Bey?

1036
02:21:20,670 --> 02:21:22,330
Come, Yaman.

1037
02:21:25,640 --> 02:21:29,640
My Bey, they brought Erkut
Alp, he is heavily wounded.

1038
02:21:32,350 --> 02:21:35,030
Demirbüken has been martyred.

1039
02:21:35,380 --> 02:21:41,100
What are you saying, what are you saying?
Where is my Osman, where are the others?

1040
02:21:42,900 --> 02:21:44,890
They are all captives.

1041
02:21:51,400 --> 02:21:55,400
Kill me, kill me!

1042
02:21:55,820 --> 02:21:57,260
You infidel!

1043
02:22:01,660 --> 02:22:04,270
Kill me! Kill me!

1044
02:22:08,160 --> 02:22:11,840
If you don't kill me now...

1045
02:22:12,360 --> 02:22:18,120
... I will rip your lungs out and
feed them to the dogs!

1046
02:22:18,210 --> 02:22:20,210
If you want it that much-

1047
02:22:23,080 --> 02:22:24,820
Stop, Salvador!

1048
02:22:34,500 --> 02:22:35,870
Leave him.

1049
02:22:54,840 --> 02:22:57,300
Let us enjoy their deaths.

1050
02:22:57,820 --> 02:22:59,360
Princess Sofia.

1051
02:23:49,210 --> 02:23:53,210
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com